{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089495-is-the-dreaming-changeling-dynamic-the-reverse-of-the-umbra-other-dynamic","id":1089495,"title":"Is the Dreaming/Changeling dynamic the reverse of the Umbra/Other dynamic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T18:02:06-07:00","id":1089495,"title":"Is the Dreaming/Changeling dynamic the reverse of the Umbra/Other dynamic?","content":"In the Umbra you are pretty much guaranteed to be an eternally small fish in a huge ocean. Even an Archmage has to walk quietly in the Umbra because there are gods there that will eat you if you get uppity. In the Dreaming it seems the Kithain are the big fish, with the Sidhe above everyone else, and everything else is a minnow. The Tuathaan are an exception, but you are potentially more powerful than anything else in the Dreaming and the books seem to be upfront about that. Even the BIG chimera are simply low density dreams compared to even a Boggan childling. Just a pile of empty chimerical calories. Meanwhile, the Umbra has Helios, Shaman, and Gaia, and The Neverborn. An important part of Umbral life is to find a deity/totem to suck up to since you need one to have a certain status in the Umbra. Is my interpretation correct or am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 05-07-2017, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:07:40-07:00","id":1089498,"title":"","content":"Ish? But there are also extremely powerful chimera in the Dreaming that could put a severe hurting on fae. Dragons, all that kind of thing. The Dreaming itself is also.. I don't quite want to say alive? But kinda is. Basically no matter how big you are, or how big you get, the Dreaming itself is always bigger than you, in that you are made of it, and subject yet to its will and whim as far as things like the power of consequences for oathbreaking and what have you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also Changelings, the deeper into the Dreaming they go, the more their frailties magnify and their personalities warp and exaggerate beyond their ability to control. Which, is something I personally dislike as far as the Dreaming being a viable place for adventures (as combined with what amounts to an inability to remember whatever they get up to in it), but it's another barrier in the way of the kithain just rocking over things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-07-2017, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:10:43-07:00","id":1089501,"title":"","content":"Also as Dreamcraft didn't make it over into C20, unless you port it, the ability of fae to just inflict their will on the Dreaming directly or shield themselves from its effects is more limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:12:28-07:00","id":1089503,"title":"","content":"A chimera representing the 'bull-god' mythology of Mesopotamia is going to be pretty bad-ass, as would a living moon chimera, a sentient forest fire and an army of fishmen chimerae bent on tearing down merfolk civilization. Chimera can be as weak or as bad-ass as your Storyteller cares for them to be.<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> ...chimerae <i>are</i> more fragile than spirits, as they have a weakness (Banality and cold iron!) that no spirit need worry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T20:25:16-07:00","id":1089552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089495-is-the-dreaming-changeling-dynamic-the-reverse-of-the-umbra-other-dynamic?p=1089503#post1089503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A chimera representing the 'bull-god' mythology of Mesopotamia is going to be pretty bad-ass, as would a living moon chimera, a sentient forest fire and an army of fishmen chimerae bent on tearing down merfolk civilization. Chimera can be as weak or as bad-ass as your Storyteller cares for them to be.<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> ...chimerae <i>are</i> more fragile than spirits, as they have a weakness (Banality and cold iron!) that no spirit need worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some spirits do have some fairly hard-hitting bans, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:27:28-07:00","id":1089718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089495-is-the-dreaming-changeling-dynamic-the-reverse-of-the-umbra-other-dynamic?p=1089552#post1089552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some spirits do have some fairly hard-hitting bans, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But for the purposes of my argument I was explaining that chinerae needn't be weaklings. You are nevertheless right, however: spirits sometimes DO have powerful restrictions on them and their behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:29:57-07:00","id":1089768,"title":"","content":"As of C20, there are also bygones in the Dreaming, too. Rather than being purely dreamed beings, they're beings with their own objective reality who sought shelter in the Dreaming after the Mythic Age.<br /> <br /> There are other things beside the Kithain which are immortal or long-lived, and which are more powerful than chimerae: Adhene, Thallain, perhaps other fae creatures we've yet to discover.<br /> <br /> It's perhaps more useful to think of chimerae as the flora and fauna of the Dreaming, with the Kithain, Gallain and Thallain the 'people' of the Dreaming. There are higher order spirits and even gods, as well, but these are the Tuatha and Fomorians, and they're located out of reach of the Kithain who, as beings forever tied to the mortal world now, just don't get to be part of those higher orders of being any more.<br /> <br /> But the True Fae of Arcadia very well might be akin to the higher spirit orders. They might be very different to kithain as we understand them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}